  "_note": "Measurements of source/groom-bride.webp (1536 \u00d7 1024 px) for scripts/couple/derive.ts. Each half: its x span, the box around its printed title, the person's outline, and its cards in the order they appear: a rough clockwise quad (snapped to the white frame), an optional tape strip, or for the gaming cluster a traced outline; column l or r on the phone page. grow: px added around each removed title. cardGrow: px added around each removed card (past its drop shadow); close: px of the gaps between neighbouring cards that are closed. pillars: boxes at the page edges never borrowed from. grain: fine noise in the rebuilt title areas. bokeh: how the area behind the cards is rebuilt (scripts/couple/bokeh.ts) \u2014 reach: px over which the picture beside an area softens into it; blur: radius of that softening; grain: fine noise inside; ramp: px over which the leaf-green shade builds up from the area's edge; shade, minLight, shadeMix: how deep, how dark and how strongly that green replaces the colours around; leaves: sharp leaves cut from the picture itself (density: how many; radius: size range in px; minFoliage: least share of a cut-out's source that is leaf; fringe: px they hang past the edge; fringeShare: share of them that hang past it); palms: palm fronds cut from the picture (mask boxes in `palms` above); donor: banana leaves cut from the temple picture (radius, scale, density, tilt, minFoliage, rows they may fall in, and far: the big out-of-focus ones behind). shadowReach, shadowDark: how far (px) and how dark (brightness) the dark strips beside a card's area may be to join it. extend: the zoom-out \u2014 rows added above the couple by stretching the band of sky between the garlands and the heads (per half: the band's first and last picture row; feather: px each edge of the band eases over).",
